# THREE conditions, not two -- (a) splits into (a-bare) [H1 ASSUMED 0, un-derived] + (a-rich) [here].
def colour_quartic_charge_handle() -> dict:
    """[DERIVED handle + LOCATED-GAP (iii)] §9.6/§20.2 (TASK H2): the holomorphic coefficient of
    H1's reduction has a CHARGE HANDLE, and the question of whether the §9.6 rich (hysteretic)
    branch sets it to zero is LOCATED at a single gated property of the reactive barrier face.

    THE 3-DIM QUARTIC SPACE on C^3 (cubic-point-group invariants): {(Σ|c|²)², Σ|c|⁴, |Σc²|²}.
    U(3) (→ su(3) → octet → C_A/C_F=9/4) needs BOTH coefficients to vanish:
      (a) the holomorphic |Σc²|² coefficient  -- THIS task (H2),
      (b) the Σ|c|⁴ coefficient (= H1's fourth-moment B; the −4/+4 e₄-bond cancellation) -- H1.

    THE CHARGE HANDLE (under the redundant global phase exp(θE), c_a → e^{iθ}c_a):
      • Σ|c_a|²  (modulus)            : charge 0   -- U(3)-invariant
      • Σ c_a²   (holomorphic bilinear): charge 2
      • |Σc_a²|² (holomorphic quartic) : charge 0   -- SO(3)-invariant, U(3)-BREAKING
    CONSEQUENCE: the α phase-invariance premise gives U(3) at QUADRATIC order (a bare charge-±2
    Σc_a² is forbidden there) but does NOT extend to the quartic -- |Σc²|² is charge-0, so
    phase-invariance does not forbid it. Quartic U(3) is an INDEPENDENT dynamical question:
    it holds iff the trapping couples only to the charge-0 modulus, not the charge-2 bilinear.

    WHY IT IS (iii), NOT INSTALLABLE (the fourth colour package):
      • |Σc²|² depends only on the RELATIVE phases φ_a−φ_b (invariant under the global phase).
      • The SETTLED linear/decoherence face (Goldstone/Adler-zero, WP-DC2/IX4) constrains the
        OVERALL phase only (derivative coupling); it does NOT reach the relative phases. Forbidding
        |Σc²|² would need an un-grounded per-colour U(1)^3 (only the global U(1)=exp(θE) is grounded,
        cl41_phase_is_external_u1) -- assuming it is the install.
      • "within-B=0" is the BARYON/winding sector (π_3(S^3)=Z), a DIFFERENT B from H1's fourth-moment
        B; it says nothing about the holomorphic direction. "B=0 well" ⇏ "flat in |Σc²|²".
      • A barrier (τ_mem=τ_wave·e^{S/ℏ}, MemoryKernel.HYSTERETIC) is necessarily ANHARMONIC, so the
        |Σc²|² question lives exactly at the rich branch's defining quartic level -- the REACTIVE face
        (the barrier action S), which the paper records as the #1 open item ("DC2 does not touch it").

    THE LOCATED SUB-QUESTION (a sharpened component of the #1 gap): does the §9.6 rich-branch reactive
    barrier V(c_a) (quartic) DEPEND ON THE RELATIVE meta-time (E-)phases of the colour amplitudes
    (couple to |Σc²|², λ_holo ≠ 0 → U(3) breaks) or is it RELATIVE-PHASE-FLAT (λ_holo = 0 →, with H1's
    B=0, U(3) → su(3) → 9/4)? This is the relative-phase-locking content of the gated barrier action S.

    THREE-CONDITION ACCOUNTING (cross-build correction, Coordinator reconciliation): the colour quartic's
    TOTAL holomorphic coefficient is a SUM of two distinct sources, both gated on Sec 9.6:
        lambda_holo,total = lambda_holo,bare(Sec 10.3 STATIC Skyrme projection)  [H1: ASSUMED 0, NOT derived
                                                                                  -- the 'forced form' install]
                          + lambda_holo,rich(Sec 9.6 RICH-branch reactive barrier) [H2: the located gap here].
    The external-U(1) does NOT forbid the holomorphic term in EITHER source (|Σc²|² is charge-0). So
    colour-U(3) (-> su(3) -> 9/4) needs ALL THREE: (b) B=0 [H1, gated on e4-bond participation];
    (a-bare) lambda_holo,bare = 0 [H1, un-derived -- a STILL-OPEN H1 item, not closed by 'given H1'];
    (a-rich) lambda_holo,rich = 0 [H2, the relative-phase-flatness of the rich-branch barrier, located here].
    H2 pins ONLY the third. 'given H1' delivers only (b), gated -- it does NOT supply (a-bare).

    CONDITIONAL DISCRIMINANT ON THE FORK (the value of the reduction, stated honestly): GIVEN (b) B=0 AND
    (a-bare) lambda_holo,bare = 0, the colour sector becomes a sharp discriminant on the rich branch via H2:
      rich barrier relative-phase-FLAT (lambda_holo,rich = 0) ⇒ U(3)/octet/9-4 AND rich branch CONFIRMED by
                                                                colour (outcome i);
      rich barrier relative-phase-LOCKING (lambda_holo,rich != 0) ⇒ U(3) breaks on the rich branch ⇒ rich
                                                                branch DISFAVOURED (toward fading) OR colour
                                                                is not su(3) (outcome ii).
    The bare coefficient (a-bare) remains a separate un-derived H1 item; do NOT let it disappear into this
    reduction (it would be a cross-build U(3)-by-construction).

    GATE: qcd_collider_phenomenology() STAYS RAISING (octet/9-4 face would un-gate on (i);
    asymptotic freedom / Bjorken remain open regardless). Returns the verified handle + the gap."""
    import cmath, random  # lazy; keep module import numpy-free (numpy not needed here)
    E = wave_E5()
    # verify the charge weights directly: exp(θE) ~ multiply each c_a by e^{iθ} in R[E]≅C
    random.seed(0)
    def _charge(fn, n):
        for _ in range(200):
            c = [complex(random.uniform(-1, 1), random.uniform(-1, 1)) for _ in range(3)]
            th = random.uniform(-3.14159, 3.14159)
            cth = [cmath.exp(1j * th) * z for z in c]
            if abs(fn(cth) - cmath.exp(1j * n * th) * fn(c)) > 1e-9:
                return False
        return True
    mod   = lambda c: sum(abs(z) ** 2 for z in c)
    holo  = lambda c: sum(z ** 2 for z in c)
    holo2 = lambda c: abs(sum(z ** 2 for z in c)) ** 2
    return {
        "E^2 == -1 (single global phase exp(θE))": (E * E) == (-1.0) * SCALAR,
        "quartic space (3-dim)": "{(Σ|c|²)², Σ|c|⁴, |Σc²|²}",
        "charge(Σ|c|²) == 0": _charge(mod, 0),
        "charge(Σc²) == 2": _charge(holo, 2),
        "charge(|Σc²|²) == 0": _charge(holo2, 0),
        "phase-invariance forbids |Σc²|²?": False,  # charge-0 => allowed; NOT forbidden
        "|Σc²|² symmetry": "SO(3)-invariant, U(3)-breaking; depends only on relative phases φ_a−φ_b",
        "quadratic level": "modulus-only AUTOMATICALLY (bare Σc² is charge ±2, forbidden) — not where U(3) is decided",
        "H2 question (quartic)": "does the rich-branch barrier couple to charge-2 Σc² (|Σc²|²≠0 → U(3) breaks) "
                                 "or only charge-0 Σ|c|² (→ with H1 B=0, U(3)→su(3)→9/4)?",
        "verdict": "(iii) LOCATED-GAP: gated on the relative-phase-locking content of the §9.6 rich-branch "
                   "REACTIVE barrier (the barrier action S) — the #1 gap's reactive face, which DC2/IX4 do not touch. "
                   "NOT installable (within-B=0 / metastable-well labels do not fix the holomorphic direction).",
        "conditional discriminant": "given B=0 (H1, gated) AND the bare Sec 10.3 holomorphic coeff = 0 "
                                    "(H1, UN-DERIVED -- a separate open item), colour-U(3) <=> the rich-branch "
                                    "barrier is relative-phase-flat; pinning it confirms the rich branch (i) or "
                                    "disfavours it / breaks su(3) (ii).",
        "three open conditions for colour-U(3)": "(b) B=0 [H1, gated on e4-bond participation]; (a-bare) "
                                    "lambda_holo,bare=0 [H1, ASSUMED not derived -- still open]; (a-rich) "
                                    "lambda_holo,rich=0 [H2, located = relative-phase content of the rich barrier]. "
                                    "H2 pins only the third; do not fold (a-bare) into 'given H1'.",
        "gate": "qcd_collider_phenomenology() stays RAISING (octet/9-4 un-gates on (i); asymptotic freedom/Bjorken remain).",
    }


