def _sqrt_masses(Lam, b, eps, psi):
    """Brannen 2-harmonic sqrt-mass triplet: sqrt(m_n) = Lam[1 + b cos(phi_n - psi)
    + eps*b cos(2 phi_n - psi)], phi_n = 2pi n/3.  (eigenVALUES on the Z3 orbit.)
    CONVENTION (2026-08-13, ADJUDICATION2 keeper C1): this is the psi-FORM second harmonic
    cos(2*phi - psi), one of FOUR epicycle variants in the corpus; the 2psi-form PHASE
    STRUCTURE cos(2*(phi - psi)) is derivation-backed (mass_measure_from_omega, FORM only).
    On the Z3 orbit both collapse into the first harmonic (cos(2phi_n-psi) = cos(phi_n+psi)),
    so psi is NOT FIXED BY THE MASS SPECTRUM (mass-gauge), and variants inter-convert UNDER A
    RE-FIT of (b, eps) -- the same (b, eps) may NOT be carried across forms. The
    mass-observable content is the invariant (A, psi_inv) -- see
    brannen_z3_harmonic_collapse_invariant."""
    return [Lam*(1 + b*math.cos(2*math.pi*n/3 - psi)
                 + eps*b*math.cos(2*(2*math.pi*n/3) - psi)) for n in range(3)]


def brannen_z3_harmonic_collapse_invariant():
    """[DERIVED-A GIVEN the two-harmonic form -- generic N-point aliasing, NOT a Clifford/D4
    identity: collapse identity + phasor resultant + degeneracy witness + convention
    inter-convertibility, all checked below -- applied to banked FIT inputs]
    §19.7 psi-repair (ADJUDICATION2 2026-08-03 keeper C1; executed 2026-08-13; §8a-round
    scope/provenance fixes applied same day).

    THE COLLAPSE (exact): on the Z3 orbit phi_n = 2*pi*n/3, 2*phi_n = -phi_n (mod 2*pi), so
        cos(2*phi_n - psi) = cos(phi_n + psi)          [psi-form second harmonic]
        cos(2*(phi_n - psi)) = cos(phi_n + 2*psi)      [2psi-form second harmonic]
    -- at N=3 the second harmonic ALIASES into the first. Three sqrt-masses carry only a mean
    + ONE complex first harmonic (3 dof), so at fixed Lam the parametrization (b, eps, psi) is
    a 3->2 map: psi is NOT FIXED BY THE MASS SPECTRUM (mass-gauge; degenerate with (b, eps);
    two distinct triples exhibited below hit the SAME three values -- one with eps = 0). psi
    still parameterizes MODEL observables (eigenvector orientation in the CKM constructions);
    only its mass-spectrum reading falls.

    THE INVARIANT: phasor addition b*cos(phi-psi) + eps*b*cos(phi+psi) = A*cos(phi - psi_inv):
        psi_inv = atan2((1-eps)*sin(psi), (1+eps)*cos(psi))     [branch-correct; the bare
                  tan psi_inv = ((1-eps)/(1+eps))*tan psi form is off by pi when cos psi < 0]
        A = b*sqrt(((1+eps)*cos psi)^2 + ((1-eps)*sin psi)^2)
    verified below over b in [0.1,3], eps in [-3,3] (incl. eps > 1 and eps < 0), psi in
    [-pi,pi]. (A, psi_inv) = the 3-point DFT of the values themselves -> computable MODEL-FREE
    from the masses; reparametrization- and convention-independent.
    PRIOR ART (credited; discharges the worklist F3 Zenczykowski duty at this site):
    Zenczykowski, Phys. Rev. D 86 (2012) 117303 (arXiv:1210.4125) states the N=3
    parameter-counting non-observability, and its Eq. (12) IS the model-free closed form
        tan(delta_f) = sqrt(3)*(sqrt(m2)-sqrt(m1)) / (2*sqrt(m3)-sqrt(m2)-sqrt(m1))
    (verified below == the DFT phase); Zenczykowski, Phys. Rev. D 87 (2013) 077302
    (arXiv:1301.4143) makes the delta_D-vs-delta_L non-equality comparison itself; Koide,
    arXiv:hep-ph/0005137 (2000) 'Quark and Lepton Mass Matrices with a Cyclic Permutation
    Invariant Form' is the PRIORITY for the circulant/single-harmonic Z3 parametrization
    (priority correction 2026-08-18, prior-art pass RUL-050: Brannen's 2006 self-published
    note is an INDEPENDENT RE-NOTICING of the charged-lepton case that pinned 2*eta = sqrt(2)
    and the phase numerically, NOT the origin of the form; the split is stated in
    Rivero & Gsponer arXiv:hep-ph/0505220 p. 8 and by Zenczykowski); Koide,
    J. Phys. G 34 (2007) 1653 is the refereed entry point for Brannen's result and carries
    the single-harmonic Z3 form as the parameter-counting consequence; Rosen,
    Mod. Phys. Lett. A 22 (2007) 283 is
    the all-delta_f-equal hypothesis -- the class of claim struck here, already problematized
    by Zenczykowski 2012. Internal antecedents: koide_from_c / dft_K_from_r already encode
    amplitude-as-invariant.

    DOWN SECTOR, MODEL-FREE (the canonical number): the 3-point DFT of the engine's own three
    down sqrt-masses (PDG_QUARK_MASSES; assignment b->n=0, s->n=1, d->n=2 -- the ordering the
    banked fit realizes) gives psi_inv,d = 6.294 deg, A_d = 1.546135 -- no b, no eps, no psi,
    no fit. ADJUDICATION2's quoted 6.294 deg is CORRECT AS STATED (model-free from the
    masses). The fit-parametrization route (banked b_d = 1.172, eps_d = 0.344 at the fit's own
    psi_d = 12.755 deg) gives 6.305 deg -- the 0.011 deg difference is the <0.2% fit residual,
    not a different object. Either way psi_inv,d != delta_L = 12.732 deg: the old
    'psi_d ~= 12.76 deg ~= the lepton delta_L' clause compared a mass-gauge parameter to
    delta_L and is STRUCK. SCHEME + PROVENANCE DISCIPLINE (coordinator-corrected 2026-08-13):
    (a) psi_inv,d = 6.294 deg is the invariant of the MS-BAR INDICATOR TRIPLE -- the input
    set is MIXED-SCHEME (m_d, m_s MS-bar at 2 GeV; m_b at m_b), the value is
    scheme-dependent (~5.8 deg at all-at-2-GeV, m_b(2 GeV) ~= 4.84 GeV, checked below; up
    to ~8.5 deg across quark-mass scheme choices), and quark masses are INDICATORS/witnesses,
    never verifiers (canon §5; quark_mass_reconstruction's mass-verifier principle). Do NOT
    read psi_inv,d as 'the observable down phase' -- it is the indicator-triple invariant.
    (b) The corpus's CREDITED down phase is the HADRON-ROUTE band |delta_d| ~= 5.8-8.5 deg
    (probe 5 / ADJUDICATION2: d->s->b steps through three hadron environments with the
    environment/binding axes subtracted -- hadron frequencies ONLY, N57-free; a DIFFERENT
    construction of the same referent: forced-amplitude K = 3/2 single-harmonic on the
    generation steps, delta_d = F(Db/Ds)), bracketing Zenczykowski's 4/27 rad = 8.488 deg
    (the worklist 1/27-ladder line). The hadron route OUTRANKS the indicator invariant
    ontologically -- only hadron masses are physical. (c) The strike is OVER-DETERMINED:
    both routes land far below delta_L = 12.73 deg (MS-bar indicator 6.29 deg; hadron band
    <= 8.5 deg). Lepton boundary: eps = 0 makes psi_inv = psi identically -- for the lepton
    triple the resultant phase IS delta_L, so delta_L remains an observable of the three
    lepton masses (leptons are physical). CROSS-ROUTE: A_d = 1.546 => K_down =
    koide_from_c(A_d) = (2 + A^2)/6 = 0.7318 (reciprocal 1.367 -- ADJUDICATION2's
    independently derived K_down): the invariant quark/lepton asymmetry is the AMPLITUDE
    (vs lepton A = sqrt(2), K = 2/3). NOTED-NON-COINCIDENCE (canon guard, banked as NOTHING):
    psi_inv ~= delta_L/2 numerically only because (1-eps_d)/(1+eps_d) = 0.488 ~= 1/2 with tan
    near-linear at these angles.

    CONVENTION (scoped 2026-08-13): the corpus runs FOUR epicycle variants --
      (i)   psi-form  +eps*b*cos(2*phi - psi)          [quark_brannen_table/_sqrt_masses]
      (ii)  2psi-form -sqrt(eps)*cos(2*(phi - psi))    [_sqrt_m / companion _metatime_sqrt_m]
      (iii) 2psi-form -(sin^2 tau/2)*cos 2(phi - psi)  [mass_measure_from_omega r^2 expansion]
      (iv)  2psi-form +(sin^2 tau/2)*cos 2phi          [companion epicycle_reading_dependent]
    The sign difference (iii) vs (iv) is the unpinned e4-dip axis: which projection leg
    carries the tilt is a modeling choice. What mass_measure_from_omega DERIVES is the
    2psi-form PHASE STRUCTURE (deferent and epicycle sharing psi) -- 'derivation-backed' is
    scoped to the FORM only, not to any amplitude convention or coefficient sign. On the Z3
    orbit all variants are INTER-CONVERTIBLE UNDER A RE-FIT of (b, eps) (phasor matching,
    witnessed below); the SAME (b, eps) may NOT be carried across forms (reading the table's
    (b_d, eps_d) in form (ii) distorts the down sqrt-mass ratios by x4.6 -- checked below).
    (A, psi_inv) is the convention-independent content. COEFFICIENT CONSTRAINT (located gap,
    ledger N60): the r^2-orbit behind (iii) caps the orbit-invariant amplitude at A <= 1
    (max exactly 1.0 at the r^2 >= 0 saturation, checked below), while the banked amplitudes
    are A_lepton = sqrt(2) and A_d = 1.546 -- NO r^2-orbit realizes the banked triples;
    brannen_amplitude's c is a projection RATIO (unbounded), so R-064's geometry can host
    c = sqrt(2) where the r^2-orbit cannot."""
    np = __import__("numpy")
    phis = [2*math.pi*n/3 for n in range(3)]
    # (1) the collapse identities, both conventions, dense psi grid
    worst_c1 = max(abs(math.cos(2*p - s) - math.cos(p + s))
                   for p in phis for s in np.linspace(0, 2*math.pi, 721))
    worst_c2 = max(abs(math.cos(2*(p - s)) - math.cos(p + 2*s))
                   for p in phis for s in np.linspace(0, 2*math.pi, 721))
    assert worst_c1 < 1e-12 and worst_c2 < 1e-12, "Z3 second-harmonic collapse must be exact"

    def orbit_psi_form(b, eps, psi):
        return _sqrt_masses(1.0, b, eps, psi)   # single source: the table's psi-form helper

    def dft_invariant(vals):
        m = sum(vals)/3.0
        z = sum((v/m - 1.0)*complex(math.cos(p), math.sin(p)) for v, p in zip(vals, phis))*(2.0/3.0)
        return abs(z), math.atan2(z.imag, z.real)

    # (2) phasor resultant + closed formula; eps domain [-3, 3] (incl. eps > 1 and eps < 0)
    rng = np.random.default_rng(20260813)
    for b, eps, psi in rng.uniform([0.1, -3.0, -math.pi], [3.0, 3.0, math.pi], (300, 3)):
        A_f = b*math.hypot((1+eps)*math.cos(psi), (1-eps)*math.sin(psi))
        if A_f < 1e-6:
            continue                             # resultant ~ 0: phase undefined, skip
        vals = orbit_psi_form(b, eps, psi)
        A, pinv = dft_invariant(vals)
        pinv_f = math.atan2((1-eps)*math.sin(psi), (1+eps)*math.cos(psi))   # branch-correct
        assert abs(A - A_f) < 1e-9 and abs((pinv - pinv_f + math.pi) % (2*math.pi) - math.pi) < 1e-9, \
            "phasor resultant psi_inv = atan2((1-eps)sin psi, (1+eps)cos psi) must hold"
        assert max(abs(v - (1 + A*math.cos(p - pinv))) for v, p in zip(vals, phis)) < 1e-9, \
            "three orbit values must equal the single resultant harmonic"

    # (3) DOWN, MODEL-FREE (the canonical number): DFT of the engine's own sqrt-masses
    #     (assignment b->n=0, s->n=1, d->n=2 -- the ordering the banked fit realizes);
    #     MIXED-SCHEME inputs (m_d, m_s at 2 GeV; m_b at m_b) -- INDICATORS, not verifiers.
    d_m, s_m, b_m = PDG_QUARK_MASSES["down"]
    A_free, pinv_free = dft_invariant([math.sqrt(b_m), math.sqrt(s_m), math.sqrt(d_m)])
    assert abs(math.degrees(pinv_free) - 6.294243) < 1e-4, \
        "model-free psi_inv,d = 6.294 deg (mixed-scheme; ADJUDICATION2's figure, correct as stated)"
    # Zenczykowski PRD 86 (2012) 117303 Eq. (12): independent closed form, must equal the DFT
    r1, r2, r3 = sorted(math.sqrt(x) for x in (d_m, s_m, b_m))
    delta_zen = math.atan2(math.sqrt(3.0)*(r2 - r1), 2*r3 - r2 - r1)
    assert abs(delta_zen - pinv_free) < 1e-12, "Zenczykowski Eq.(12) == the 3-point DFT phase"
    # alternate scheme point (all-at-2-GeV, m_b(2 GeV) ~= 4.84 GeV): scheme-dependence made explicit
    _, pinv_2gev = dft_invariant([math.sqrt(4840.0), math.sqrt(s_m), math.sqrt(d_m)])
    assert 5.7 < math.degrees(pinv_2gev) < 5.9, "all-at-2-GeV scheme point: psi_inv,d ~= 5.81 deg"
    # the STRIKE is over-determined: MS-bar indicator points AND the hadron-route candidate
    # rational point (4/27 rad = 8.488 deg, bracketed by the credited 5.8-8.5 deg band) all
    # land far below delta_L
    dL_deg = math.degrees(2.0/9.0)
    assert all(abs(x - dL_deg) > 4.0 for x in
               (math.degrees(pinv_free), math.degrees(pinv_2gev), math.degrees(4.0/27.0))), \
        "psi_inv,d != delta_L on both routes (the struck ~=delta_L clause)"
    # cross-route: the invariant amplitude feeds the banked Koide identity K = (2+c^2)/6
    K_down = koide_from_c(A_free)
    assert abs(K_down - 0.731756) < 1e-4 and abs(1.0/K_down - 1.367) < 1e-3, \
        "A_d => K_down = 0.7318 (reciprocal 1.367 -- ADJUDICATION2's independently derived K_down)"

    # fit-parametrization route (secondary): banked (b_d, eps_d) at the fit's own psi_d
    from scipy.optimize import minimize
    b_d, eps_d = 1.172, 0.344
    tgt = np.sort(np.sqrt(np.array(PDG_QUARK_MASSES["down"]))); rd = np.log(tgt[1:]/tgt[0])
    def loss(psi):
        v = np.sort(np.abs(np.array(orbit_psi_form(b_d, eps_d, float(psi)))))
        return 1e9 if v[0] < 1e-12 else float(np.sum((np.log(v[1:]/v[0]) - rd)**2))
    best = min(((p, loss(p)) for p in np.linspace(0, 2*math.pi, 400)), key=lambda t: t[1])
    r = minimize(lambda x: loss(x[0]), [best[0]], method="Nelder-Mead",
                 options=dict(xatol=1e-12, fatol=1e-16))
    psi_fit = float(r.x[0]) % (2*math.pi)
    A_d, pinv_d = dft_invariant(orbit_psi_form(b_d, eps_d, psi_fit))
    assert 12.70 < math.degrees(psi_fit) < 12.80, "down psi-form fit lands ~12.755 deg"
    assert abs(math.degrees(pinv_d) - math.degrees(pinv_free)) < 0.05, \
        "fit-route psi_inv (6.305 deg) differs from the model-free 6.294 deg only by fit residuals"
    # lepton boundary: eps = 0 -> psi_inv = psi identically (delta_L stays a mass observable)
    _, pinv_lep = dft_invariant(orbit_psi_form(math.sqrt(2), 0.0, 2.0/9.0))
    assert abs(pinv_lep - 2.0/9.0) < 1e-9, "eps=0 (leptons): psi_inv = psi identically"

    # (4) mass-gauge witness: two distinct triples, same three values
    vals1 = orbit_psi_form(b_d, eps_d, psi_fit)
    vals2 = orbit_psi_form(A_d, 0.0, pinv_d)                    # eps re-gauged to ZERO
    assert max(abs(x - y) for x, y in zip(vals1, vals2)) < 1e-9, \
        "two distinct (b,eps,psi) triples must reproduce the SAME three sqrt-masses"

    # (5) inter-convertibility UNDER RE-FIT: psi-form -> 2psi-form phasor matching at psi'=30deg.
    #     The re-fit (b', eps') != (b_d, eps_d): the SAME (b, eps) may NOT be carried across forms.
    psip = math.radians(30.0)
    det = -math.cos(psip)*math.sin(2*psip) - math.sin(psip)*math.cos(2*psip)
    bx = (-A_d*math.cos(pinv_d)*math.sin(2*psip) - A_d*math.sin(pinv_d)*math.cos(2*psip))/det
    cx = (math.cos(psip)*A_d*math.sin(pinv_d) - math.sin(psip)*A_d*math.cos(pinv_d))/det
    vals3 = [1 + bx*math.cos(p - psip) + cx*math.cos(2*(p - psip)) for p in phis]
    assert max(abs(x - y) for x, y in zip(vals1, vals3)) < 1e-9, \
        "a RE-FIT 2psi-form triple must reproduce the psi-form orbit values exactly"
    A3, pinv3 = dft_invariant(vals3)
    assert abs(A3 - A_d) < 1e-9 and abs(pinv3 - pinv_d) < 1e-9, \
        "(A, psi_inv) must be convention-independent (a DFT of the values)"
    # carrying the SAME (b, eps) across forms is NOT legal: down sqrt-mass ratio distorts x4.6
    v_2psi = [1 + b_d*math.cos(p - 2.0/9.0) - math.sqrt(eps_d)*math.cos(2*(p - 2.0/9.0)) for p in phis]
