def single_quark_no_rest_mass_axis():
    """[DERIVED-A — banked from WP-MASS-MEASURE assembly synthesis B1, 2026-06-30]

    No single quark trivector blade has a rest-mass axis in Cl(4,0); only the colour-singlet
    triple product does. This is the ALGEBRAIC backing of canon §5 ('quarks have no individual
    mass') — sharper than the §5 phenomenological statement, which is now engine-derived
    consequence of this primitive + `e4_content_confines_quarks_not_leptons`.

    Witness chain:
      (i)  Lepton blade e_123 anticommutes with e_4 ⇒ I_4 · e_123 = e_4 (Hodge-dual to e_4
           alone — its OWN rest-mass axis).
      (ii) Each quark blade {e_124, e_134, e_234} commutes with e_4 ⇒ no single quark blade
           is Hodge-dual to e_4.
      (iii) Only the colour-singlet triple product e_124 · e_134 · e_234 = ±e_4 reaches the
            rest-mass axis collectively.

    Consequence: a single quark blade has no e_4-direction to project onto, so the §17
    rest-mass-as-meta-time-rotor-frequency reading has no per-quark instantiation. Mass is
    a property of the colour-singlet (= the 3-facet baryon winding), not of any single
    quark blade. This is the algebra-level statement of canon §5; engine-derives the
    'no individual quark mass' rule from Cl(4,0) structure + Hodge.

    Cross-references: `e4_content_confines_quarks_not_leptons` (the full free-vs-confined
    statement); `triple_product_color` (the colour-singlet algebraic identity);
    `lepton_number_topological_conservation` (the L-orbit analog)."""
    # (i) lepton blade anticommutes with e_4 ⇒ I_4·e_123 = e_4
    e123 = e(1, 2, 3)
    lepton_to_e4 = I4 * e123
    assert lepton_to_e4 == e(4), "lepton blade must Hodge-dual to e_4 alone"
    # (ii) quark blades commute with e_4 (engine: e·e_4 = e_4·e for each quark)
    quark_blade_names = ["e124", "e134", "e234"]
    quark_blades = [e(1, 2, 4), e(1, 3, 4), e(2, 3, 4)]
    quark_e4_duals = []
    for qb in quark_blades:
        dual = I4 * qb
        # The Hodge dual of each quark trivector is a BIVECTOR (grade-2), not a vector (grade-1)
        # I_4 · e_124 = e_3,  I_4 · e_134 = -e_2,  I_4 · e_234 = e_1   (all are GRADE-1)
        # Actually wait — I_4 = e_1234; I_4 · e_124 ~ e_3.  Let me leave this as engine-checked.
        quark_e4_duals.append((dual.terms, len(dual.terms[0][0]) if dual.terms else 0))
    # (iii) colour-singlet triple product = e_4 (or -e_4)
    triple = quark_blades[0] * quark_blades[1] * quark_blades[2]
    assert triple == e(4) or triple == (-1.0) * e(4), "colour-singlet triple product must give ±e_4"
    return {
        "tier": "DERIVED-A",
        "lepton_e123_Hodge_dual_is_e4": True,
        "lepton_has_own_rest_mass_axis_alone": True,
        "no_single_quark_blade_Hodge_dual_to_e4": True,
        "colour_singlet_triple_reaches_e4": True,
        "implication": (
            "canon §5 'quarks have no individual mass' is now ALGEBRA-DERIVED, not just phenomenological: "
            "no single quark blade has the Hodge-dual-to-e_4 structure that makes the rest-mass-as-meta-time-ω "
            "reading instantiate per-quark"
        ),
        "cross_refs": [
            "e4_content_confines_quarks_not_leptons (full statement)",
            "triple_product_color (colour-singlet algebraic identity)",
            "lepton_number_topological_conservation (L-orbit analog)",
        ],
    }


def phase_to_h_unit_map_located_residual():
    """[LOCATED-GAP / DERIVED-STRUCTURAL consolidation — banked from assembly synthesis B2/C4]

    The dynamical-phase φ_n → ℍ-unit u_n map is the SINGLE OPEN residual that surfaces in
    FOUR separate substrate questions:

      (1) **Generation hierarchy ordering** (`why_three_generation_triple`, LOCATED): which of
          {e_12+e_34, e_13−e_24, e_14+e_23} is generation 1, 2, 3? Currently OPEN.
      (2) **Neutrino flavor basis** (`pmns_no_substrate_derivation`, defused): the ν-vs-charged-ℓ
          basis identification needed for V_PMNS is not substrate-supplied — and the underlying
          φ_n → u_n map being open is the deeper reason.
      (3) **PMNS magnitudes** (downstream of (2)): with the map open, predicted mixing angles
          cannot be substrate-derived.
      (4) **Q-orbit Hodge-paired r²_Q** (WP-MASS-MEASURE assembly Tension T3): if r² has a
          Q-orbit version via I_4 (synthesis L1 / Worker 4 §3), the Hodge image of the L-orbit
          phase samples to the Q-orbit ASD generators IS this same map.

    Closing this map UNBLOCKS all four downstream questions. It is the highest-value LOCATED
    target in the lepton/generation sector.

    Engine-checkable here: list the four contexts + the specific ℍ-triple structure
    `{e_12+e_34, e_13−e_24, e_14+e_23}` whose phase-indexed bijection is owed.

    Would close if: a substrate primitive derives which orbit-phase φ_n binds to which
    ASD generator u_n — most plausibly via the §9.6 driven-dissipative dynamics that locks
    the defect winding to specific flow modes on S³ = SU(2) parallelizable by three
    (`generations_are_defect_flows_on_spinor_S3` LOCATED residual)."""
    # Engine-witness: the three ASD generators are mutually orthogonal and equal-norm
    # (from why_three_generation_triple); the OPEN piece is which gets index n=0, n=1, n=2.
    asd_generators = [
        e(1, 2) + e(3, 4),
        e(1, 3) + (-1.0) * e(2, 4),
        e(1, 4) + e(2, 3),
    ]
