def front_phase_handoff_selects_winding_axis() -> dict:
    """[DERIVED-A (the ideal-projection dichotomy: exact, all three B_a, orthogonal
    line basis, generic angles) + DERIVED-CONDITIONAL (the axis SELECTION, forced by
    self-coherence with banked Part-B QM -- conditions named) + FRAMING (the
    reconciliation notes)] -- WP-MASS-MEASURE / R-123 residue (iii): WHICH unit
    carries the front mass phase k_4 in the observer's complex structure?
    ANSWER: the defect's own winding direction B_a -- and there is no E -> B_a
    'conversion' to construct: the observer-visible mass phase never leaves B_a.
    (2026-07-02)

    THE QUESTION (R-123 residue (iii), verbatim): the rotor axis u_hat is meta-time/
    central content (an H unit or E = I_4 e_5); the KG reduction's i is the
    transverse defect-selected B_a (SB.3.1 centralizer, R-020). The restriction
    identity R-123(i) is axis-independent, so it cannot resolve which unit the
    OBSERVER's k_4 phase rides. The owed construction was framed as a hand-off
    E -> B_a.

    THE MOVE. Take the banked defect ansatz (SA.3 form, with B_a in the
    SB.3.1/R-020 grade-2 winding reading -- see C1):
        Psi_a = F(chi) . B_a . s_0 . q_h(tau_5),  s_0 = (1 + e_4)/2 (SA.5.4),
        q_h = exp(u_hat omega tau_5 / 2),  B_a in the L-orbit triplet,
    and project the tau_5-history onto the OBSERVER'S FORCED COMPLEX LINE
        L = Psi_0 . span{1, B_a},   Psi_0 = B_a s_0
    (the {1, B_a} subalgebra is R-020's engine-exact centralizer intersection --
    the observer has no other complex line to read). Ask, axis by axis: does the
    front periodicity appear in L as a PURE U(1) phase (what R-017's KG one-particle
    mode IS), or as something else?

    THE EXACT DICHOTOMY (engine, all three B_a in {e12, e13, e23}, generic angle;
    the line basis {Psi_0, Psi_0 B_a} is exactly orthogonal):
      - u_hat = +/- B_a: the history STAYS IN L EXACTLY (out-of-line = 0);
        in-line coordinates (cos(th/2), +/- sin(th/2)) = a pure U(1) phase; the
        extracted phase-advance rate (doubling convention, same extraction as
        R-123/R-125) is EXACTLY +/- omega; on the wavefront lock, k_4 = omega/c_meta
        in the observer's i = B_a. CONVENTION-FREE: B_a commutes with s_0 and
        itself, so left and right action coincide for the winner.
      - u_hat in the L-orbit but not +/- B_a (the other two H units, and any
        mixture): the history LEAVES L (out-of-line > 0) while staying INSIDE the
        Cl(4,0) ideal -- the k_4 periodicity reads as PRECESSION into the
        orthogonal (spin-flip) state sector, with the L-shadow a pure AMPLITUDE
        modulation cos(th/2), phase coordinate identically 0. A partial axis
        (mixture) gives a reduced-rate phase PLUS precession -- also not the pure
        KG mode. (Reviewer bonus check: the losers leave the line under LEFT
        action too -- the exclusion is not convention-fragile beyond the
        winner/E convention-free cases.)
      - u_hat = E = I_4 e_5 (central): the history leaves the Cl(4,0) ideal
        ENTIRELY (nonzero e_5-blade content -- engine); its ideal shadow is the
        same amplitude modulation cos(th/2). An E-carried front phase would
        present to the observer as DENSITY NODES along x_4, not a propagating
        phase. E central => left = right: convention-free exclusion.

    THE SELECTION (DERIVED-CONDITIONAL). Banked Part B (R-017 + R-020/R-021 + the
    empirical face: matter waves interfere as propagating phases) says the
    one-particle mass label is a pure U(1) phase in the observer's complex line.
    By the dichotomy, that is possible for EXACTLY u_hat = +/- B_a. So, GIVEN the
    banked ansatz and the banked QM reading, the front mass phase is carried by
    the defect's own winding direction -- the SAME blade R-020's centralizer
    forces as the observer's i. V2 S3.2's 'two faces of one defect' becomes exact:
    ONE blade B_a, two roles (topological winding direction; the QM complex unit
    carrying the mass phase). The sign choice -B_a is the conjugate branch --
    coherent with R-126's -omega family. Conditions, named:
      (C1) the separable defect ansatz Psi_a = F B_a s_0 q_h in the SB.3.1/R-020
          GRADE-2 form -- B_a a grade-2 L-orbit winding bivector, the object
          R-020's centralizer computation actually uses (reviewer fix: SA.3's
          prose glosses B_a as a grade-3 type blade -- a pre-existing corpus
          DOUBLE-USE of the symbol B_a, flagged for a disambiguation pass; this
          primitive's blade IS R-020's). Same idealization class as R-123/R-125's
          C2. The axis MENU tested is u_hat in span{L-orbit} plus {E} plus (sweep
          hardening 2026-07-02) the three Q-ORBIT axes incl. the Hodge dual of B_a --
          ALL Q-orbit axes leave the lepton line (amplitude-only shadow), so the
          selection u_hat = +/-B_a survives the extended menu;
      (C2) the hand-off criterion = banked Part-B QM: the observer's one-particle
          mode is a pure phase in the forced {1, B_a} line (R-017/R-020; the
          empirical-coherence face: interferometry sees phases, not node
          patterns or spin precession standing in for mass);
      (C3) L-orbit / lepton-sector scope (R-020's scope); the baryon Q-orbit
          analog is named, not built.

    CONSEQUENCE FOR RESIDUE (iii): RESOLVED-AS-SELECTION. There is no owed E->B_a
    conversion mechanism -- within the banked ansatz the observer-visible mass
    phase never leaves B_a. E keeps its banked roles (the GLOBAL/colour complex
    structure, wave_E_complex_structure; the canon's own partition says QM i =
    e12-class, global i = E) but is EXCLUDED as the observer-visible mass-phase
    carrier.

    RETROACTION (coherence dividends, stated not re-banked):
      - R-125's axis-split weakness (the E-axis symmetry premise was NOT banked)
        becomes MOOT for the physical mass phase: with u_hat = +/- B_a selected,
        the mass-phase collective mode rides the BANKED left-Spin(4) bivector
        branch. The E-i/E-ii routes remain recorded for the hypothetical E-axis
        case only.
      - R-126's label table: the physical mass axis sits in the u_hat-commutant
        class that reads +omega (and -B_a in the conjugate class) -- consistent.
      - Residue (ii)'s (H2) target sharpens: the one-particle pole candidate is
        specifically the B_a-phase mode in the observer's line.

    RECONCILIATION NOTE (flagged for review, not hidden): sakharov_xi_minimal_
    coupling's docstring glosses the rotor mass as 'the central-E U(1) phase ...
    a SEVENTH direction, distinct from the 6 grade-2 bivectors'. This result puts
    the OBSERVER-VISIBLE mass phase on a bivector direction (B_a). NOT a
    contradiction of that primitive's load-bearing content, on this reading: the
    xi-protection needs NO STATIC POTENTIAL on the 6 Goldstone (bivector shift)
    directions; a mass phase along B_a is a TIME-DEPENDENT ROTATION ALONG a flat
    direction (kinetic, Q-ball-style -- exactly WHY R-125's collective mode is
    exact and unlifted), not a potential lift of it. The xi conclusion (xi = 0
    protected; no 1/6 branch) is untouched; only the informal 'seventh direction'
    GLOSS of which unit carries omega is superseded for the observer-visible face.
    If review finds this reconciliation wrong, the selection here downgrades to
    CANDIDATE and the tension escalates -- recorded so the check is explicit.

    STILL OPEN (honesty): a substrate-DYNAMICAL derivation that the defect's
    meta-time rotor axis locks to its winding direction (here it is selected by
    consistency with the banked QM reading, not derived from the EOM); the baryon
    Q-orbit analog (C3); residue (ii)'s (H1)+(H2), unchanged.

    WOULD CHANGE IF: an EOM-level derivation of the axis lock upgrades the
    selection to DERIVED-dynamical; a Q-orbit construction extends it to baryons;
    an observed matter-wave mass signature that is NOT a pure propagating phase
    (density nodes / mass-correlated spin precession) would falsify the selection
    criterion's empirical face.
    """
    import itertools as _it
    import numpy as np

    ONE = SCALAR
    s0 = 0.5 * ONE + 0.5 * e(4)
    E5 = e(1, 2, 3, 4, 5)
    KEYS = [()] + [tuple(c) for k in range(1, 6)
                   for c in _it.combinations(range(1, 6), k)]

    def _coords(x):
        return np.array([x.coeff(k) for k in KEYS])

    def _mvnorm(x):
        return sum(abs(c) for _, c in x.terms)

    def _rotor(u, th):
        return math.cos(th / 2.0) * ONE + math.sin(th / 2.0) * u

    s0_idempotent = _mvnorm(s0 * s0 - s0) < 1e-14
    L_ORBIT = {"e12": e(1, 2), "e13": e(1, 3), "e23": e(2, 3)}
    omega, c_meta, th_gen = 0.937, 1.31, 1.234   # generic (Phase F)

    per_Ba = {}
    for Ba_name, Ba in L_ORBIT.items():
        Psi0 = Ba * s0
        v1, v2 = _coords(Psi0), _coords(Psi0 * Ba)
        line_orthogonal = abs(float(v1 @ v2)) < 1e-14
        Q, _ = np.linalg.qr(np.stack([v1, v2], axis=1))

        def _out(x):
            c = _coords(x)
            return float(np.linalg.norm(c - Q @ (Q.T @ c)))

        def _inline(x):
            c = _coords(x)
            g = np.array([[v1 @ v1, v1 @ v2], [v2 @ v1, v2 @ v2]])
            return np.linalg.solve(g, np.array([v1 @ c, v2 @ c]))

        others = [u for n, u in L_ORBIT.items() if n != Ba_name]
        mix_perp = (1.0 / math.sqrt(2.0)) * (others[0] + others[1])   # pure-perp mixture
        mix_part = (1.0 / math.sqrt(2.0)) * (Ba + others[0])          # partial B_a component
        axes = {
            "+B_a": Ba, "-B_a": -1.0 * Ba,
            "H_perp_1": others[0], "H_perp_2": others[1],
            "H_mix_perp": mix_perp, "H_mix_partial": mix_part, "E": E5,
            # sweep hardening 2026-07-02: the Q-orbit axes (incl. the Hodge dual of
            # B_a) close the menu hole C1 named — all must leave the lepton line
            "Q_14": e(1, 4), "Q_24": e(2, 4), "Q_34": e(3, 4),
        }
        rows = {}
        for name, u in axes.items():
            Psi = Psi0 * _rotor(u, th_gen)
            a, b = _inline(Psi)
            e5c = math.sqrt(sum(c * c for k, c in zip(KEYS, _coords(Psi))
                                if 5 in k))
            rows[name] = {"out_of_line": _out(Psi), "inline_a": float(a),
                          "inline_b": float(b), "e5_content": e5c}

        # phase advance for the winner (doubling convention), front-lock reading
        def _phase(t5):
            aa, bb = _inline(Psi0 * _rotor(Ba, omega * t5))
            return 2.0 * math.atan2(bb, aa)

        w_ext = (_phase(0.5 + 1e-6) - _phase(0.5)) / 1e-6
        # left action = right action for the winner (commutes) and for E (central)
        lr_winner = _mvnorm(_rotor(Ba, th_gen) * Psi0 - Psi0 * _rotor(Ba, th_gen)) < 1e-13
        lr_E = _mvnorm(_rotor(E5, th_gen) * Psi0 - Psi0 * _rotor(E5, th_gen)) < 1e-13

        cos_half, sin_half = math.cos(th_gen / 2), math.sin(th_gen / 2)
        per_Ba[Ba_name] = {
            "line_orthogonal": line_orthogonal,
            "rows": rows,
            "winner_phase_rate": w_ext,
            "left_equals_right_for_winner_and_E": lr_winner and lr_E,
            "dichotomy_ok": (
                rows["+B_a"]["out_of_line"] < 1e-13
                and abs(rows["+B_a"]["inline_a"] - cos_half) < 1e-12
                and abs(rows["+B_a"]["inline_b"] - sin_half) < 1e-12
                and rows["-B_a"]["out_of_line"] < 1e-13
                and abs(rows["-B_a"]["inline_b"] + sin_half) < 1e-12
                and all(rows[n]["out_of_line"] > 0.1 for n in
                        ("H_perp_1", "H_perp_2", "H_mix_perp", "H_mix_partial", "E",
                         "Q_14", "Q_24", "Q_34"))
                and all(abs(rows[n]["inline_b"]) < 1e-12 for n in ("Q_14", "Q_24", "Q_34"))
                and abs(rows["H_perp_1"]["inline_b"]) < 1e-12
                and abs(rows["H_perp_2"]["inline_b"]) < 1e-12
                and abs(rows["H_mix_perp"]["inline_b"]) < 1e-12      # pure-perp: amplitude only
                and rows["H_perp_1"]["e5_content"] < 1e-13   # precession stays in Cl(4,0)
                and rows["H_perp_2"]["e5_content"] < 1e-13
                and rows["E"]["e5_content"] > 0.1            # E leaves the Cl(4,0) ideal
                and abs(rows["E"]["inline_b"]) < 1e-12
                and 0.0 < abs(rows["H_mix_partial"]["inline_b"]) < sin_half  # partial: reduced rate + precession
            ),
        }

    all_ok = all(v["dichotomy_ok"] and v["line_orthogonal"]
                 and abs(v["winner_phase_rate"] - omega) < 1e-5
                 and v["left_equals_right_for_winner_and_E"]
                 for v in per_Ba.values())

    assert s0_idempotent, "s_0 = (1+e_4)/2 must be idempotent"
    assert all_ok, "the hand-off dichotomy must be exact for all three B_a"

    return {
        "outcome": ("RESIDUE (iii) RESOLVED-AS-SELECTION -- the observer-visible front mass "
                    "phase is carried by the defect's own winding direction +/-B_a (the same "
                    "blade R-020 forces as the QM i); other H axes read as spin precession, "
                    "the central E leaves the Cl(4,0) ideal (density-node shadow); no E->B_a "
                    "conversion mechanism is owed"),
        "tier": ("DERIVED-A (ideal-projection dichotomy, exact, all three B_a) + "
                 "DERIVED-CONDITIONAL (the selection; C1 banked SA.3 ansatz, C2 banked "
                 "Part-B QM pure-phase criterion + its empirical face, C3 L-orbit scope) + "
                 "FRAMING (xi-gloss reconciliation: rotation ALONG a flat direction is "
                 "kinetic, not a potential lift -- xi = 0 protection untouched)"),
        "worklist_ref": "WP-MASS-MEASURE residue (iii); companion Section 12 row '1/2 boundary' -> resolved at Class 1",
        "s0_idempotent": s0_idempotent,
        "per_Ba": per_Ba,
        "k4_reading": ("with u_hat = B_a the front phase advance is exactly omega "
                       "(doubling convention); on the lock x_4 = c_meta tau_5 the observer "
                       "reads exp(B_a k_4 x_4)-type phase with k_4 = omega/c_meta -- the "
                       "R-017 label in the R-020 complex line"),
        "retroaction": ("R-125's unbanked E-axis premise MOOT for the physical mass phase "
                        "(the winner rides the banked left-Spin(4) bivector branch); R-126 "
                        "labels consistent; residue (ii) (H2) target = the B_a-phase mode"),
        "still_open": ("EOM-level axis-lock derivation (selection is consistency-forced, "
                       "not dynamical); baryon Q-orbit analog; residue (ii) (H1)+(H2)"),
        "would_change_if": ("EOM-level axis lock derived => upgrades to DERIVED-dynamical; "
                            "Q-orbit construction => extends to baryons; a matter-wave mass "
                            "signature that is not a propagating phase => falsifies the "
                            "criterion's empirical face"),
    }


